<VI _name="RemoteVI Service Client.vi" description="Services one WebSocket client without blocking (docs\5Cprotocol.md sections 4-6). Reads whatever bytes are waiting (TCP Read\2C immediate mode\2C timeout 0\3B error 56 means nothing waiting\2C any other error means the peer is gone and sets closed)\2C appends them to rx buffer and decodes every complete frame with RemoteVI WS Decode Client Frame.vi. A text frame goes through RemoteVI Parse Input.vi\3A an ack raises acked to max(acked\2C seq) when seq is not ahead of the client's seq\3B mouse and key messages first update mods (RemoteVI Track Modifiers.vi) and\2C when they changed and no popup is open\2C write them into the key state of LabVIEW's UI thread (RemoteVI Apply Modifiers.vi - LabVIEW reads Shift/Ctrl/Alt with GetKeyState\2C which posted messages do not update)\2C then are translated (RemoteVI Translate Input.vi with geo\2C popup = popups.windows not empty\2C and tracking in = LabVIEW holds the mouse capture\2C RemoteVI Mouse Captured.vi) and posted to the window hWnd (RemoteVI Post Input.vi\2C which - while a popup is open - moves the invisible popups so that the clicked point lies under the host cursor\2C never moving the cursor\2C and waits until the popups change\2C at most 300 ms\3B the displacement it used travels on to the next message and out in popups out)\3B a minimized panel is restored first (RemoteVI Restore If Minimized.vi). No VI Server call\2C so servicing goes on while an open LabVIEW popup blocks the UI thread\3B the server loop supplies geo\2C hWnd and popups from its cache. clicked? tells the server loop that a message which may open a LabVIEW popup (anything but WM_MOUSEMOVE and WM_MOUSEWHEEL) was posted\2C so it holds its VI Server calls back until the popup has had time to appear. A ping is answered with a pong\3B a close frame with a close frame (1000)\3B a binary or fragmented message with close 1008\3B a protocol violation with the decoder's close code - each sets closed. Consumed bytes leave rx buffer. A click on a popup is posted no sooner than 350 ms after the popup was first seen open (popup since)\3A LabVIEW ignores a click on a ring menu that arrives within about 250 ms of opening it (measured with posted messages\3A 200 ms ignored\2C 250 ms chosen). A client that closes with modifiers written is released (mods set back to 0\2C unless a popup is open). Mouse and key messages go to the window RemoteVI Route Input.vi picks among windows (docs\5Cprotocol.md section 7)\3B key window - the window the client last pressed a button in - travels from message to message. A client already closed is passed through untouched. TCP errors only set closed\3B error out carries the errors of restoring the window and posting input.">
